ple gets to  recycle components which in turn leads  to a lower manufacturing cost and a  higher profit at a lower price this  brings us to our second reason which is  some good old-fashioned money higher  profits  revenue is very good business it means  that income does not stop for apple this  is likely going to increase revenue over  time now you've seen peloton they're  trying this now according to  counterpoint research the average iphone  sale price is about 825  that means apple is generating a bit  over 800 from the typical iphone  customer every three years keep in mind  that this is only if a typical iphone  customer chooses to get a new iphone  every three years i know people that are  still on the iphone 7. so you might want  to take this estimate with the grain of  salt now in the bloomberg article mark  german did a rough breakdown of how much  apple could make using the new proposed  subscription model let's take the new  iphone 13 lineup as an example the  iphone 13 pro and pro max cost around  799.99 and one thousand ninety nine  dollars respectively using the same  monthly subscription price points that  the report used which in case you're  wondering are thirty five dollars forty  five dollars and fifty dollars for each  of the models here's how much apple  would generate over three years from the  monthly subscription compared with the  upfront price iphone 13 35 a month 1 260  over three years instead of 799  iphone 13 pro 45 dollars a month  six hundred twenty dollars instead of  nine hundred ninety nine dollars iphone  thirteen pro max fifty dollars a month  one thousand eight hundred dollars  instead of one thousand ninety nine  dollars see how much their profit  margins improved factor in the steady  stream of recyclable components they  would get in addition to these increased  sales profits and you can see why a  subscription model is actually a better  option for apple themselves better  option for consumers  this doesn't mean that the subscription  model is bad news for the consumer in  fact i actually believe that this might  be good news for both the consumer and  apple hear me out let's say that you  change your iphone after every three  years to do that you have to spend eight  hundred dollars now imagine that every  year you get the latest iphone and  instead of fishing out twenty four  hundred dollars you just have to pay  somewhere around twelve hundred dollars  that sounds like a steal to me the  latest and greatest iphone always in  your pocket for a small monthly payment  doesn't sound too bad you can just skip  a few expensive lattes a month and that  would cover the cost of your new phone  applecare  according to some sources it is expected  that this subscription will also come  with some of apple's other online  services included the entire package  might include extra icloud storage an  apple tv subscription and even applecare  these services will be available at a  reduced price in addition to the actual  phone and are expected to take apple's  profits even further up issues  sounds great right new iphone cheaper  too plus you're helping out with the  environment at the same time so what's  the catch well first of all this model  completely removes the ownership part of  well owning a phone out of the equation  and at the same time opens up questions  regarding privacy what would happen if  you don't pay the fee do they just take  the phone away or is there a fine all  these are questions that arise with the  subscription model but until more  information comes out there's sadly  nothing anyone can say in case you're  worried about the high price with no  actual ownership you should keep in mind  that it doesn't really matter you just  subscribe and at a price lower than what  it would cost you to buy the iphone you  can use it essentially as your own i  think that's a great idea and apple  could really hit a home run with this  one expected pricing  now what is the expected pricing of  these subscriptions i would place my  money on a number below 35 dollars a  month for the simplest plan and less  than 50 a month for the most premium  plan these numbers might be even lower  since apple's profit margin really is  just that high with these phones the  best deal in my opinion would be the one  that comes with a suite of apple  services most importantly apple care  included the rates for these would be  discounted in addition to the already  discounted prices of the phones and it  would overall be a great deal for the  consumer and depending on the price a  subscription might end up being cheaper  than buying multiple apple products the  iphone has historically been apple's  biggest money maker so any move that  improves the sales and the profit  margins of the iphone are a welcome  change following bloomberg's report  apple shares climbed to a session high  on thursday and closed up 2.3 percent at  174.7 cents apple has now posted eight  straight days of increases its longest  streak since november i can't say  definitively that this new service will  be worth it since there has been  absolutely no news about the expected  price but if the price turns out to be  in the same ballpark as most people  think it is we might just see a turn in  the tide when it comes to phone  ownership expected arrival date no one  at apple is talking about when the  subscription service might arrive  although rumors are that we might just  see it at apple's next launch event you  might be thinking that it's too early  for that but actually no the idea for a  subscription service for apple isn't  that foreign sanford c bernstein and  company analyst tony sekinagi pitched  the idea of hardware subscription in  2016. many customers would struggle to  think of a single possession they use  more than their iphone he said moreover  the cost of the iphone is a relative  bargain versus other services for which  consumers willingly pay if it turns out  to be true apple wants to let you  subscribe to its hardware products just  like you would subscribe to icloud apple  music or apple tv plus google has  actually been using this for their  corporate use based chromebooks so if  they can do not apple all in all apple  just announced what might be the biggest  news they've had since well they  announced the iphone apple is coming out  with a subscription model for their new  iphones for what is expected to be a  monthly payment of 35 dollars you will  be leased the latest iphone this move is  expected to reduce e-waste and help  apple skyrocket their profits the report  of this news helped apple record their  eighth day of consecutive rise in the  stock market and if all goes well we  might see this model being released for  use in at least america at apple's next  launch event fingers crossed this will  live up to the hype click a video on the  screen for more content like this and  i'll see you there
 

